![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `agent__intent` field must be explicitly removed from the `args` object after extraction. This fulfills the promise made in the system prompt ("it is stripped before tool execution") and prevents potential validation errors in tools that do not expect this metadata field. I've also updated the logic to handle the stripping even if `callID` is missing.

```javascript
function extractAndStoreIntent(callID, args) {
  if (!args || typeof args !== "object") return undefined;

  const raw = args[INTENT_FIELD];
  if (typeof raw !== "string") return undefined;

  // Strip the field so it doesn't reach the tool execution
  delete args[INTENT_FIELD];

  const intent = raw.trim();
  if (!intent) return undefined;

  if (callID) {
    intentByCallId.set(callID, intent);

    // Prune old entries to prevent unbounded memory growth
    if (intentByCallId.size > 5000) {
      const keys = Array.from(intentByCallId.keys());
      for (const k of keys.slice(0, 2500)) {
        intentByCallId.delete(k);
      }
    }
  }

  return intent;
}
```

