This function uses `localDisplayName` to construct the target for `sendMessage`. User display names can contain spaces or special characters, which can break the command format. It's more robust to use the `contactId`, which is a unique and safe identifier. The type casting can also be simplified.

```typescript
  private handleContactConnected(event: SimplexEvent): void {
    const contact = (event as any).contact;
    const name = contact?.localDisplayName ?? "unknown";
    this.logger.info(`New contact connected: ${name}`);

    if (this.config.autoAcceptContacts && this.config.welcomeMessage) {
      const contactId = contact?.contactId;
      if (contactId !== undefined) {
        this.sendMessage(`@${contactId}`, this.config.welcomeMessage);
      } else {
        this.logger.warn("Could not send welcome message: contactId is missing.");
      }
    }
  }
