_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Initial connection failure still schedules a reconnect via the `onclose` handler.**

When `onerror` fires on the first connection attempt (`reconnectAttempts === 0`), `this.disconnect()` calls `this.ws.close()`, which triggers `onclose`, which calls `this.scheduleReconnect()`. The initial promise correctly rejects, but a reconnect timer is silently started. In `main()` this is moot because `process.exit(1)` follows, but if `SimplexAdapter` is used as a library, the caller gets both a rejected promise AND an unwanted background reconnect loop.


<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix — skip reconnect when initial connect was rejected</summary>

```diff
