In @.agents/scripts/simplex-bot/src/index.ts around lines 187 - 198, The onerror
handler can trigger disconnect() during the first connection attempt which then
fires onclose and starts scheduleReconnect() despite the initial connect promise
being rejected; change the logic so that when onerror sees reconnectAttempts ===
0 it prevents scheduling a reconnect — for example, set a flag (e.g.,
this.initialConnectFailed) or call a new method to disable reconnects before
calling this.disconnect() in the onerror handler, and update the onclose handler
(or scheduleReconnect) to check that flag (or reconnectAttempts state) and skip
calling scheduleReconnect(); modify the handlers: onerror, onopen (which resets
reconnectAttempts), disconnect, and onclose/scheduleReconnect to respect that
flag/state so no background reconnect is started after the initial connect
