_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**`onerror` suppresses reconnect for ALL errors, including mid-session network drops.**

Setting `intentionalDisconnect = true` in `onerror` prevents the `onclose` handler from scheduling a reconnect in every error scenario — not just the initial connection failure. After a successful connection (where `reconnectAttempts` is reset to `0` in `onopen`), a transient network error or server restart will silently close the connection with no recovery.

The fix should distinguish between an initial connect failure (no reconnect desired, promise must reject) and a mid-session error (reconnect desired):

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix — guard intentionalDisconnect on initial connect only</summary>

```diff
         this.ws.onerror = (event: Event) => {
           this.logger.error("WebSocket error", event);
-          if (this.ws) {
-            this.intentionalDisconnect = true;
-            this.ws.close();
-            this.ws = null;
-          }
-          reject(new Error(`Failed to connect to ${url}`));
+          if (this.reconnectAttempts === 0) {
+            // Initial connection failed — suppress the reconnect that onclose
+            // would otherwise schedule, then reject the connect() promise.
+            if (this.ws) {
+              this.intentionalDisconnect = true;
+              this.ws.close();
+              this.ws = null;
+            }
+            reject(new Error(`Failed to connect to ${url}`));
+          }
+          // Mid-session errors: let onclose fire naturally so scheduleReconnect runs.
         };
```

Note: `reconnectAttempts` is incremented in `scheduleReconnect()` and reset to `0` in `onopen`, so `=== 0` correctly identifies the very first connection attempt.
