The recursive call in `generateId` to handle ID collisions could theoretically lead to a stack overflow if there are many collisions in a row. While extremely unlikely with a 16-bit ID space and few pending requests, it's a best practice to avoid unbounded recursion. A `while` loop is a more robust pattern for this.

```typescript
  private generateId(): string {
    let id: string;
    do {
      const bytes = new Uint8Array(2);
      crypto.getRandomValues(bytes);
      id = Array.from(bytes)
        .map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0"))
        .join("");
    } while (this.pending.has(id));
    return id;
  }
